    "result_text": "The full suite passes: **290 tests, 0 failures**.\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented audit logging for successful owner creation in `OwnerRestControllerV1.addOwner`.\n\nChanges to `src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/rest/controller/v1/OwnerRestControllerV1.java`:\n\n1. Added a dedicated SLF4J logger named `AUDIT`:\n   ```java\n   private static final Logger auditLogger = LoggerFactory.getLogger(\"AUDIT\");\n   ```\n\n2. After a successful `saveOwner`, log the authenticated user plus the new owner's id and membership number:\n   ```java\n   Authentication authentication = SecurityContextHolder.getContext().getAuthentication();\n   String user = (authentication != null) ? authentication.getName() : \"anonymous\";\n   auditLogger.info(\"Owner created by user={} id={} membershipNumber={}\",\n       user, owner.getId(), owner.getMembershipNumber());\n   ```\n\nThe log line is emitted only after the create succeeds (it comes after `saveOwner` and never runs when validation/duplicate/quota checks throw). It records the authenticated principal name, the new owner id, and the membership number \u2014 matching the spec.\n\nThe provided acceptance test `Cp19Tests` (which captures the `AUDIT` logger and asserts the message contains `acceptance-admin` and the new owner id) passes, along with all existing owner controller tests and the full 290-test suite.",
